# README  - summarize role of each .conf file supporting package.env
#
# ghostscript-fix.conf ------------- relax selected compiler warnings/errors
# crossbuild-perl-fix.conf --------- override/de-confuse perl compiler/linker flags during cross-builds 
# j4_makeopts.conf ----------------- limit package build concurrency to MAKEOPTS="-j4"
# nobin_features.conf -------------- force source builds by disabling getbinpkg and userpriv
# no_collision-protect.conf -------- disable collision protection for packages that intentionally share files
# mysql-with-protobuf-bundled.conf - force MySQL to build and use its bundled protobuf implementation
# lang-en_US-UTF-8.conf ------------ force LANG=en_US.UTF-8 for the selected package
# bind_ldflags.conf ---------------- add BIND build-tree library paths with -Wl,-rpath-link for transitive linking
# j1_makeopts.conf ----------------- serialize package builds (prohibit parallel) with MAKEOPTS="-j1"
# linker_assist.conf --------------- add --copy-dt-needed-entries to help resolve transitive linker dependencies
# nodist_features.conf ------------- disable distcc (FEATURES=-distcc)
# nobin_features.conf -------------- deprecated (**)
#     ** source-only installation policy is enforced separately by
#     EMERGE_DEFAULT_OPTS --usepkg-exclude
#     (in joetoo-platform-meta make.conf template)
#
# tools/test-harness - test all packages that have been accumulated in package.env with nodist_features.conf
#   to help determine if they are in fact still incompatible with distcc
#
# Policy - use each .conf to express a single feature/configuration policy
# SOP - when muliple policies should be enforced for a given package, include the
#   package on one line in package.env which lists each .conf above naming a policy
#   that should be enforced for that package
#
# Testing - for develompent, the tools/ directory provides several testing tools -
#
#-----[ test-harness ]---------------------------------------------------------------
# test-harness - test packages for distcc compatibility
# ckage-env # ./tools/test-harness -h
#  ✨ usage: test-harness [-h] [-r l|<timestamp>] [-f /path/to/file] [pkg [pkg ...]]
#  * Options --
#   -f /path/to/file ..........: set FILE mode (build pkglist from file contents)
#   pkg [pkg [pkg ...] ........: set FILE mode (incl pkg in pkglist)
#   -r l[atest]|<timestamp> ...: set RESUME mode (resume process from persisted state)
#   -I ........................: set INTERACTIVE mode (prompt y|n|s before test run)(default)
#   -N ........................: set NON-INTERACTIVE mode (do not prompt for approval) (faster)
#   -v ........................: increase verbosity
#   -q ........................: decrease verbosity
#   -h ........................: help (show this message)
#  * Note --
#   test-harness default behavior is to build pkglist from developer's package.env
#   Only one method of specifying an alternate source for pkglist is allowed
#     -f /path/to/file, pkg pkg pkg (arg list), or package.env (default, no arg)
#   pkg must be a valid [<category>/]<package>
#   -f and pkg [pkg] are exclusive (rejected as error)
#   -f and -r <arg> are exclusive ("last one wins")
#   for -r <timestamp>, format is YYYYMMDD-HH:MM:SS or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
# Outcome classifications:
#   succeeded   - target emerge succeeded; remote distcc compilation verified
#   unvalidated - target emerge succeeded; remote distcc compilation not verified
#   retry       - Phase 1 target emerge failed; pending dependency preparation
#   prepared    - Phase 2 dependency preparation succeeded; pending Phase 3
#   blocked     - Phase 2 dependency preparation failed
#   failed      - Phase 3 target emerge failed after dependencies were prepared
#   excepted    - package excluded from testing by explicit policy
#
#-----[ monitor-test-harness ]---------------------------------------------------------------
# monitor-test-harness - in a separate terminal, monitor progress of test-harness
#   (also includes options to clean up or archive test results)
# #  ✨ usage: sudo monitor-test-harness [-c a|i|<ts>] [-a a|l|<filter>] [-w] [-v]
#  * Options --
#   -w ..............: set WATCH mode (run continuously; summarize)
#   -v ..............: set VERBOSE mode (run once; show all data) (default)
#   -c a|i|<ts> .....: set CLEANUP mode (all|interactive|timestamp)
#   -a a|l|<filter> .: set ARCHIVE mode (all|latest|<archive_filter>)
#   -h ..............: help (show this message)
#  * Note --
#   -w, -v, -c <arg>, and -a <arg> are exclusive; "last wins"
#   cleanup and archive filenames all resemble test-harness-status-20261009-18:55:57
#   -c must be followed by <arg> which can be
#     a|all meaning delete everything matching '*test-harness*' template 
#     i|interactive meaning clean interactively; confirm each deletion
#     <timestamp> meaning delete everything matching template and <timestamp>
#     <timestamp> must be in the format YYYYMMDD-HH:MM:SS or YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
#   -a must be followed by <arg> which can be
#     a|all meaning archive everything matching '*test-harness*' template 
#     l|latest meaning archive everything matching the latest timestamp
#     <filter> meaning archive files matching <filter>, which can be --
#       like "<timestamp>" meaning archive all matching timestamp, or
#       like "<pattern>-<timestamp>" lets you archive one file matching <pattern>-<timestamp>
#       (but it can match several (recocmmended to use e.g. "status" for such one-file pattern)
#       n.b. filter must always include a complete <timestamp> in one of the forms above
#     monitor-test-harness must be run by root
#     users needing archive access must be in the wheel group
#
#-----[ test-harness-common-functions ]---------------------------------------------------------------
# test-harness-common-functions - includes --
#    [helper] functions used by both test harness and monitor-test-harness
#    functions that can be used from cmdline for test result evidence collection
#
# latest_ebuild() - collect actual ebuild for pkgs listed as args
#    (to determine appropriate disposition for packages placed in categories
#     unvalidated (succeeded, but no evidence that distcc helped), failed, blocked)
#
# latest_logfile() - collect the latest portage build log_file for pkgs listed as args
#
# dump_fileset() - dump the content of each file in the timestamped test fileset
#
# latest_ts() - get the most recent timestamp from test-harness output filesets
#
# list_ts() - list the timestamps of all test-harness output filesets
#
# discover_and_validate_ts() - [helper] discover latest timest; validate; assign to global $ts
#
# normalize_timestamp() - [helper] if $1 is in "YYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" form, convert to "YYYYMMDD-HH:MM:SS"
#
# dump_status() - [hrlprt] list current content of global status variables
#    (phase, pkglist_count, prog_start, cur_pkg_name, cur_pkg_start)

